TASK=75-ringrtc-signal-calls
STEP=ringer-arbiter
STATUS=in-progress
LAST_SUCCESS=Ringer built in wart-arbiter-audio (system_server Telecom-Ringer analog) + 16/16 tests. New verbs: audio-ring-start/audio-ring-stop/audio-ringer-mode. RingerMode {normal,vibrate,silent} owned by the arbiter (AudioManager analog). ring-start: per mode emits host "ringtone start"+"haptics ring-start" (normal) / "haptics ring-start" (vibrate) / nothing (silent), grabs GainTransient (pauses music), posts "Incoming call" badge (RING_NOTIF_ID 0xCA12). ring-stop (decline/miss): stops + releases focus + clears badge. call-start (answer): stop_ring first then comm mode. Ringing-owner death clears ring. Arbiter decides; owner host plays via its audio+haptics interfaces.
NOTES=FOLLOW-UPS to make it actually ring on device: (1) HOST must handle the new arbiter->host commands: "ringtone start/stop" (play/stop a ringtone via the audio interface — needs a ringtone sound source) and "haptics ring-start/ring-stop" (vibrate pattern via haptics_impl, which exists). (2) ENGINE (war.signal) must call the arbiter: audio-ring-start on incoming Offer (Ringing), audio-ring-stop on decline/miss/remote-hangup-before-answer, audio-call-start on answer, audio-call-end on end. The engine->arbiter call path: audio-call-start is currently CLI-only — need a guest-callable route (extend war:audio-focus or host-forward like focus request/abandon). Vibration HAL (haptics) + sensors already in host. Proximity-screen-off = next (arbiter comms/power + host panel blank). Prior context: Signal calls now ring real clients (urgent fix); call-log + TURN Phase A device-verified.
